Rename the worktree you run it from: change the slug it is registered under, so
it routes as <new-slug>.<domain>. A slug is a lowercase hostname label: letters,
digits and inner hyphens, at most 63 characters. The registration and index card
move to the new slug and any leftover route files are removed; `up` writes them
at the new hostname. The data directory, volumes and pinned ports are keyed by
the worktree's ID and stay as they are. It refuses a slug another worktree holds
in the same domain, the reserved slug "shared", and a worktree that still has
containers, running or stopped: run `treerig down` first.

Usage:
  treerig worktree rename <new-slug> [flags]

Flags:
      --config string   path to treerig.toml (default: nearest above cwd)
  -h, --help            help for rename

Global Flags:
      --progress mode   how to show progress: auto (redraw on a terminal) or
                        plain (one line per change) (default "auto")
  -v, --verbose         show what treerig runs, and every detail
